1. The finding and its rule

  ADV-R-14 [Major] of `measure/runs/model_guide/adversarial-bdfcfbb.json`.
  The pass record name kept the plain `RUN_SLUG`, so the routes `t/one#c`
  and `t-one#c` wrote the same `<date>-t-one-c-p1.json`, and one record
  overwrote the other.

  The orchestrator decided on 2026-11-18: the pass record name carries the
  same 12-hex `ROUTE_TAG` as the lock and the output folder. The name is
  `<date>-<slug>-<tag>-p<pass>.json`. The pass-number count and the one-pass
  "tonight" count use the slug plus tag. The record content does not change.

2. Change

  `harness/model-guide/review-run.sh` uses
  `PASS_FILE="$PASS_DIR/${DATE}-${RUN_SLUG}-${ROUTE_TAG}-p${PASS_NO}.json"`.
  The pass-number `find` pattern is `*-${RUN_SLUG}-${ROUTE_TAG}-p*.json`,
  and the no-source "tonight" pattern is
  `${DATE}-${RUN_SLUG}-${ROUTE_TAG}-p*.json`. The record content keeps the
  fields `set_id`, `route`, `pass`, `date`, `state`, `diffs`, `outputs`, and
  `errors`. The script header names the new rule.

  No test file changed.

3. Readers of pass record file names

  Green checked each reader. None parses the pass record name.
  - `review-score.ts` reads `<private>/sets/<set>/keys/<diff_id>.json` and
    `<outputs>/<diff_id>.txt`. Its `basename(name, ".json")` call reads a
    key file name, not a pass record name.
  - `preview.sh` reads the newest score file under
    `harness/model-guide/data/review-scores/` and the set manifest
    `data/sets/<set_id>.json`. It reads no pass record.
  - `guide.ts` reads the score document and its `passes` array. It reads no
    pass record file.
  - The two test helpers `passRecords` scan each JSON file with a `state`
    field. They read no name.
  - `review-run.sh` itself reads the name in the pass-number count and the
    one-pass count. Both patterns now hold the tag.

